---
import TutorialLayout from '../../../layouts/TutorialLayout.astro';
---

<TutorialLayout
  title="Custom Jinja Templates"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Tutorials', href: '/tutorials' },
    { label: 'Code Generation Workflows', href: '/tutorials' },
    { label: 'Custom Templates' },
  ]}
  prev={{ label: 'SymPy & Bode Plots', href: '/tutorials/workflows/sympy-bode' }}
  next={{ label: 'FMU Export', href: '/tutorials/workflows/fmu-export' }}
>
  <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
    Rumoca's backend system is extensible via Jinja2 templates. You can add any target language or IR format
    by writing a template that consumes the DAE IR schema. Generate code for MATLAB, Fortran, C, or any
    custom format without modifying the compiler.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Example Template</h2>
  <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-code-bg border border-border mb-6">
    <div class="text-xs font-mono text-code-text/60 mb-2">my_template.j2</div>
    <pre class="text-sm font-mono text-code-text overflow-x-auto"><code>{`# {{ model.name }} - Generated by custom template
# States: {% for s in model.states %}{{ s.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}

{% for eq in model.ode %}
d{{ eq.lhs }}/dt = {{ eq.rhs }}
{% endfor %}`}</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text mt-8 mb-4">CLI Usage</h2>
  <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-code-bg border border-border mb-6">
    <pre class="text-sm font-mono text-code-text"><code>rumoca compile model.mo --template-file my_template.j2</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
    See the <a href="https://github.com/CogniPilot/rumoca" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-teal hover:text-accent underline">
    DAE IR schema documentation</a> for the full list of available template variables.
  </p>
</TutorialLayout>
